Grove PATCH-25: host-managed wallets are not initialised by prepare, and an
auth rejection does not retry

Two defects with one symptom -- the swap node taking ten minutes to start
(and, because a stop must wait for it, ten minutes to stop) whenever ZEPH or
ZANO was enabled. Observed on the live node, 2026-09-04:

    WARNING : Can't connect to ZANO RPC: Wallet Zano RPC rejected the JWT
              (401) -- secret/salt/body-hash mismatch.  Trying again in 5
              seconds, 1/15.
    ...  10 seconds, 2/15  ...  75 seconds, 15/15  ... exiting.

That was `basicswap-prepare --addcoin=zano`. prepare's `initialise_wallets`
waits for the new coin's wallet RPC and then calls `initialiseWallet` on it.
For the two Grove host-wallet coins the wallet RPC is the HOST app's own
process (zephyr-wallet-rpc; Zano's Main simplewallet), authenticated with a
per-session secret only the supervisor knows and writes into basicswap.json
before each engine start -- prepare's own segment deliberately carries an
empty placeholder. So the wait can only ever fail, after the full retry
budget, and the coin is never added; the next start repeats it.

  bin/prepare.py, interface/prepare_util.py, interface/{zano,zephyr}/core.py
      `CoinPrepareModule.host_managed_wallet` (default False; True on the
      ZEPH and ZANO modules). `initialise_wallets` writes the chainclient
      segment for such a coin and skips the RPC wait + initialiseWallet,
      logging why. The supervisor fills in the live credentials at run time
      (it already did; this removes the step that could never succeed).

  basicswap.py
      `waitForDaemonRPC` retried EVERY exception `startup_tries` times with a
      growing delay -- 5+10+...+75 = 600 s at the defaults. A credential
      rejection ("rejected the JWT", "(401)", "Unauthorized") is
      deterministic: waiting cannot fix a wrong secret. It now logs the
      reason once and stops retrying, so a misconfigured host wallet costs
      seconds, not ten minutes. Everything else (a daemon still loading,
      a socket not yet bound) retries exactly as before.

Not an upstream candidate as written: `host_managed_wallet` is an embedder
concept (upstream has no host-owned wallet-rpc). The fail-fast half is
arguably upstream-worthy and is isolated in its own hunk.

diff --git a/basicswap/basicswap.py b/basicswap/basicswap.py
--- a/basicswap/basicswap.py
+++ b/basicswap/basicswap.py
@@ -1844,6 +1844,21 @@
                 self.coin_clients[coin_type]["interface"].testDaemonRPC(with_wallet)
                 return
             except Exception as ex:
+                # PWNDA-PATCH-25: an authentication rejection is deterministic.
+                # A wrong wallet-rpc secret does not become right by waiting,
+                # so retrying it `startup_tries` times with a growing delay
+                # (600 s at the defaults) only turns a misconfiguration into a
+                # ten-minute stall -- observed 2026-09-04 on a ZANO wallet-rpc
+                # answering 401 to every attempt. Fail at once with the reason.
+                if any(
+                    s in str(ex)
+                    for s in ("rejected the JWT", "(401)", "Unauthorized", "Unauthorised")
+                ):
+                    self.log.error(
+                        f"{Coins(coin_type).name} RPC rejected our credentials: {ex} -- "
+                        "not retrying (PWNDA-PATCH-25)."
+                    )
+                    break
                 wait_for: int = startup_delay * (1 + i)
                 if any(
                     log in str(ex)
diff --git a/basicswap/bin/prepare.py b/basicswap/bin/prepare.py
--- a/basicswap/bin/prepare.py
+++ b/basicswap/bin/prepare.py
@@ -1079,6 +1079,21 @@
             c = swap_client.getCoinIdFromName(coin_name)
             if module.provides_master_key:
                 continue
+            # PWNDA-PATCH-25: host-managed wallets (zephyr, zano) are not
+            # initialised here. Their wallet-rpc belongs to the host app and
+            # authenticates with secrets only that app knows at run time, so
+            # "wait for the wallet RPC, then initialiseWallet" is a guaranteed
+            # ten-minute retry loop ending in failure -- observed 2026-09-04 on
+            # --addcoin=zano (15 tries, growing backoff, coin never added, the
+            # same ten minutes again on the next start). The chainclient
+            # segment is still written; the supervisor fills in the live
+            # credentials before every engine start.
+            if getattr(module, "host_managed_wallet", False):
+                logger.info(
+                    f"Skipping wallet initialisation for {getCoinName(c)} (host-managed "
+                    "wallet-rpc; the supervisor provides it at run time)."
+                )
+                continue
             if coin_settings.get("connection_type") == "electrum":
                 logger.info(
                     f"Skipping daemon RPC wait for {getCoinName(c)} (electrum mode)."
diff --git a/basicswap/interface/prepare_util.py b/basicswap/interface/prepare_util.py
--- a/basicswap/interface/prepare_util.py
+++ b/basicswap/interface/prepare_util.py
@@ -154,6 +154,12 @@
     creates_wallet: bool = False  # Create the initial wallet through the core daemon
     provides_master_key: bool = False  # Other coin wallets are seeded from this coin
     reseed_note: bool = False  # Wallet can be initialised later from the ui
+    # PWNDA-PATCH-25: the coin's wallet is a HOST-managed wallet-rpc process
+    # (Grove: zephyr, zano) that prepare cannot reach -- its credentials are
+    # per-session secrets the supervisor writes into basicswap.json at run
+    # time, and the process may not be running while prepare runs. prepare
+    # writes the config segment and skips wallet initialisation for it.
+    host_managed_wallet: bool = False
 
     def getConfigSegment(self, ctx: PrepareContext) -> dict:
         raise NotImplementedError()
